      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "I ran into another issue with `guix-codesign` for rc2, this time App Armor related:\n\n```sh\nzcat /var/log/guix/drvs/2s/v5049dk6ifphfm20xp7r0rdc1vm2bv-python-signapple-3fab3bb57f227f0dd31007b417683035f5204838-checkout.drv.gz\nwarning: unable to access '/etc/gitconfig': Permission denied\nwarning: unable to access '/etc/gitconfig': Permission denied\nwarning: unable to access '/etc/gitconfig': Permission denied\nfatal: unknown error occurred while reading the configuration files\ngit-fetch: '/gnu/store/xz7xygq040vx78snmla70y03h6x9yypg-git-minimal-2.52.0/bin/git init --initial-branch=main' failed with exit code 128\n```\n\nAccording to Claude, and my own testing, adding this inside the profile `guix-helper { … }` block in `/etc/apparmor.d/guix-daemon`, helps:\n\n```\n# builtin:git-download runs git unchrooted; git treats EACCES on the\n# system config as fatal (ENOENT would be fine).\n/etc/gitconfig r,\n```\n\nI haven't filed an upstream issue yet.\n",
